  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "After Fang Yuan pulls Myriad Year Flying Warship back and begins to heal, Shen Shang laughs that Fang Yuan will not be safe if he does not attack, spreads his five fingers, presses his palm against his chest, and activates the immortal killer move Light Injuries. Inside the warship, Fang Yuan’s body shakes and he coughs out a huge mouthful of blood.",
      "chapters": [
        1907
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "house_myriad_year_flying_warship",
        "char_shen_shang",
        "sys_killer_moves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Light injuries on Shen Shang’s body also affect Fang Yuan because of mutual injuries. On Fang Yuan, because of non-conflicting dao marks, those light injuries become heavy injuries, a change of wound severity rather than a second named move. Healing killer moves also have their full effect on him, so a powerful healing method lets him recover at once.",
      "chapters": [
        1908
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shared-wounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_healing_killer_move"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Shen Shang later passes cultivation experience, killer moves, and Immortal Gu recipes to Shen Cong Sheng, he says that with heal injury Immortal Gu as the foundation he developed and created saving dead healing injuries, light injuries, heavy injuries, fatal injuries, sensory injuries, seven laborious injuries, and other killer moves.",
      "chapters": [
        1915
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
